1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,760
This presentation uses AI-generated
narration.

2
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:07,500
A pool can be ready and still be busy.

3
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:11,200
Dynamo Frontend reports readiness and
active requests.

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:16,580
Grid uses those signals to change how
it ranks serving pools, and a new

5
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:18,340
request shows the route it took.

6
00:00:19,467 --> 00:00:22,267
The recorded setup has two Kind sites.

7
00:00:23,247 --> 00:00:26,327
The Hub site contains Dynamo Pool A
and Pool B.

8
00:00:26,927 --> 00:00:29,587
The separate Site cluster contains the
Remote Pool.

9
00:00:30,387 --> 00:00:33,567
Each pool runs an independent Dynamo
Frontend with a Mocker worker.

10
00:00:34,627 --> 00:00:36,667
Grid chooses a pool or site from its
signals;

11
00:00:37,567 --> 00:00:39,187
Dynamo Frontend chooses its worker.

12
00:00:40,207 --> 00:00:44,507
Mocker returns synthetic inference
text, so this setup does not measure
GPU

13
00:00:44,507 --> 00:00:45,207
performance.

14
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:51,647
Dynamo Frontend exports real model
readiness and active-request metrics.

15
00:00:52,507 --> 00:00:55,367
Grid's versioned adapter checks
provider and model identity,

16
00:00:56,087 --> 00:00:58,887
source time, and freshness before it
compares pressure.

17
00:00:59,887 --> 00:01:02,527
Four is the configured comparison
reference in this demo.

18
00:01:03,147 --> 00:01:05,487
It is not a queue limit or measured
capacity.

19
00:01:06,127 --> 00:01:09,087
The Hub's local overlay ranks Pool A
and Pool B.

20
00:01:09,647 --> 00:01:14,027
The Site Gateway reads a separate
cross-site snapshot that includes the
Remote

21
00:01:14,027 --> 00:01:14,717
Pool.

22
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:18,694
The presenter starts pressure manually
from a pool card.

23
00:01:19,334 --> 00:01:23,654
The recording shows pressure on Pool B
and the Remote Pool while a new Site

24
00:01:23,654 --> 00:01:24,794
Gateway sample is running.

25
00:01:25,574 --> 00:01:27,214
The screen shows Frontend activity,

26
00:01:28,034 --> 00:01:28,734
candidate order,

27
00:01:29,154 --> 00:01:32,414
request counts, and the published and
consumed Hub overlay revisions.

28
00:01:33,094 --> 00:01:35,254
It does not claim a precise weighted
share.

29
00:01:36,234 --> 00:01:40,854
The recorded screen is from a
completed run on November eighth,
twenty

30
00:01:40,854 --> 00:01:41,554
twenty-six.

31
00:01:42,254 --> 00:01:44,274
Its live badges describe that capture;

32
00:01:45,094 --> 00:01:46,954
they do not describe a current
deployment.

33
00:01:48,054 --> 00:01:51,694
Mocker responses are synthetic, while
the Frontend signals are real.

34
00:01:52,494 --> 00:01:54,794
The recording does not prove GPU
saturation,

35
00:01:55,594 --> 00:01:59,014
model quality, weighted-share
precision, or live SWIM behavior.

36
00:01:59,994 --> 00:02:03,254
Frontend stage counts are not llm-d or
EPP queues.
